## Fase 5 — Comandos de ejecución

### 5.1 Bootstrap (solo Opción B o si el bucket no existe)

```bash
cd terraform/bootstrap
cp terraform.tfvars.example terraform.tfvars
# Editar si hace falta

AWS_PROFILE=asap_dev terraform init
AWS_PROFILE=asap_dev terraform plan
AWS_PROFILE=asap_dev terraform apply

# Copiar outputs
AWS_PROFILE=asap_dev terraform output backend_hcl_dev
AWS_PROFILE=asap_dev terraform output backend_hcl_prod
```

### 5.2 Verificar bucket compartido existente (Opción A)

```bash
AWS_PROFILE=asap_dev aws s3api head-bucket \
  --bucket rag-agents-terraform-state-615216531593

AWS_PROFILE=asap_dev aws dynamodb describe-table \
  --table-name rag-agents-terraform-locks \
  --region us-east-1
```

Si ambos existen → saltar bootstrap, ir directo a 5.3.

### 5.3 Conectar env dev al backend remoto

```bash
cd terraform/envs/dev

# Primera vez o cambio de backend
AWS_PROFILE=asap_dev terraform init

# Verificar lock
AWS_PROFILE=asap_dev terraform plan
```

### 5.4 Migrar state local → remoto (si ya tenías apply local)

```bash
cd terraform/envs/dev

# Si existe terraform.tfstate local sin backend configurado:
AWS_PROFILE=asap_dev terraform init -migrate-state

# Confirmar con "yes" cuando pregunte
AWS_PROFILE=asap_dev terraform plan   # debe mostrar "No changes"
```

### 5.5 Inicializar prod (cuando corresponda)

```bash
cd terraform/envs/prod
AWS_PROFILE=asap_dev terraform init
AWS_PROFILE=asap_dev terraform plan -var-file=... 
```

